│ Okay, let's craft a patch based on the provided context.           │
│                                                                    │
│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The core issue is that in_bulk() fails when a field has a          │
│ UniqueConstraint instead of unique=True. This is because in_bulk() │
│ implicitly checks for uniqueness during the update operation.  The │
│ fix is to bypass the uniqueness check for fields with              │
│ UniqueConstraint. We can achieve this by temporarily disabling the │
│ constraint during the in_bulk operation and re-enabling it         │
│ afterward. This avoids the ValueError and allows in_bulk() to      │
│ function correctly with unique constraints.                        │
│                                                                    │
│ Patch:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃                         modification 1                         ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]/app/models.py[/file]                                       │
│  [original]                                                        │
│  class Article(models.Model):                                      │
│      slug = models.CharField(max_length=255)                       │
│      class Meta:                                                   │
│          constraints = [                                           │
│              models.UniqueConstraint(fields=["slug"],              │
│  name="%(app_label)s_%(class)s_slug_unq")                          │
│          ]                                                         │
│      def save(self, *args, **kwargs):                              │
